# Open OnDemand

Open OnDemand provides browser-based access to Roary.

It allows users to work with HPC resources without requiring a traditional SSH terminal for every task.

---

## What Can You Do with Open OnDemand?

Open OnDemand can provide access to:

- File management
- Shell access
- Job monitoring
- Interactive desktops
- Jupyter
- RStudio
- VS Code
- MATLAB
- Other interactive research applications

---

## Accessing Open OnDemand

Open:

```text
OOD_URL
```

in a supported web browser.

Authenticate using your authorized FIU credentials.

---

## Files

The Files interface can be used to:

- Browse directories
- Upload files
- Download files
- Create directories
- Rename files
- Delete files
- Edit text files

---

## Shell Access

Open OnDemand can provide terminal access directly from the browser.

The shell behaves similarly to an SSH session.

---

## Interactive Applications

Interactive applications request compute resources through Slurm.

Depending on the application, you may need to select:

- Number of CPUs
- Memory
- Runtime
- Partition
- GPU resources

!!! tip "Request only the resources you need"

    Larger resource requests can sometimes take longer to schedule.

---

## Open OnDemand vs SSH

| Task | SSH | Open OnDemand |
|---|---|---|
| Terminal access | Yes | Yes |
| File management | Command line | Browser |
| Submit Slurm jobs | Yes | Yes |
| Interactive desktop | Manual | Convenient |
| Jupyter | Manual | Convenient |
| RStudio | Manual | Convenient |
| VS Code | Manual | Convenient |

---

